   "en": "The option, also called a major, is your primary area of study, with its own required courses, and it appears on your degree. A minor is a secondary area of about 30 units, equal to 10 courses, and also appears on your degree. A microprogram is a short, focused set of courses, usually nine to 15 units, that can be added to an option or minor but doesn't replace it."
