   "en": "BIO2133, Genetics (3 units), is taught in English; the French version is BIO2533. Topics: Introduction to Mendel's laws of inheritance; application of Mendelian analysis to problems in genetics including: gene mapping and linkage, molecular genetics, bioinformatics and population genetics. Prerequisites: 6 course units from BIO1131, BIO1141, BIO1150."
