   "en": "SOC2117, Sociological Theory: From 19th Century to First World War (3 units), is taught in English; the French version is SOC2517. Topics: Exploration of significant works of sociology from the 19th century to the First World War. The course shows the origins of the formation of sociological thought through several major approaches, the tensions between them, the conflicts and exclusions generated by these antagonisms. Prerequisites: (SOC1101 or SOC1104) and 15 university course units."
